.SH NAME
anx-config-alias - Create a custom binary alias/symlink for anx (e.g. for forks or personal naming)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBanx config alias  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a custom command alias pointing to the anx binary in ~/.local/bin/\&.
This allows forks or users desiring custom command names (e.g. 'myenv', 'envcli', 'dot')
to execute anx transparently under their preferred alias.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for alias


